Time Complexity:
O(n²)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
1. Traverse each index as a starting point of a subarray.
2. For every starting index, extend the subarray using another loop.
3. Count the number of zeroes in the current subarray.
4. If zeroes become greater than k, stop extending further.
5. Otherwise, update the maximum length of the valid subarray.



class Solution {
    public int longestOnes(int[] arr, int k) {
        int zeroes=0;
        int maxLen=0;
        for(int i=0; i<arr.length; i++){
            zeroes=0;
            for(int j=i; j<arr.length; j++){
                if(arr[j]==0) zeroes++;
                if(zeroes>k) break;
                else{
                    maxLen = Math.max(j-i+1, maxLen);
                }
            }
        }
        return maxLen;
    }
}
